-- title:
--   Generators of mathfrak m_R counting 𝒪-algebra maps to k[ε]
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative local ring and let $R$ be a commutative noetherian local ring equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure whose structure map $\mathcal O \to R$ is a local homomorphism. Assume that the composite of $\mathcal O \to R$ with the residue map $R \to R/\mathfrak m_R$ is surjective, so the residue field of $R$ is a quotient of $\mathcal O$. The ring of dual numbers $k[\varepsilon] = \mathrm{DualNumber}(\mathcal O/\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O})$ over the residue field $k = \mathcal O/\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ of $\mathcal O$ is made an $\mathcal O$-algebra via $\mathcal O \to k \to k[\varepsilon]$. The assertion is that there exist a natural number $m$ and elements $a_0,\dots,a_{m-1}$ of $R$, indexed by `Fin m`, such that each $a_i$ lies in $\mathfrak m_R$, such that $\mathfrak m_R$ is contained in the sum of the ideal generated by the $a_i$ and the ideal of $R$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and such that the number of $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphisms $R \to k[\varepsilon]$ equals $(\#k)^m$. Cardinalities are `Nat.card`, so an infinite set counts as $0$.
--
--   This records the equality between the cardinality of the set of $\mathcal O$-algebra maps from $R$ to the dual numbers over $k$ — the points of the reduced tangent space of $R$ over $\mathcal O$ — and $(\#k)^m$, where $m$ is the number of elements needed to generate $\mathfrak m_R$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}R$. It is used in the deformation-theoretic part of the argument, where the reduced tangent space of a deformation ring is bounded by a space of cocycle classes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_exists_generators_maximalIdeal_natCard_algHom_dualNumber_eq_pow.lean

